    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener API is complete and verified end-to-end.\n\n**What's in place:**\n- `POST/GET /links`, `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` with all specified status codes (201/200/302/404/409/422) and JSON shapes\n- `Link` model with code format (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`), uniqueness, and absolute http/https URL validation; malformed JSON rescued to 422\n- Clicks incremented atomically (`clicks = clicks + 1`) so each redirect counts exactly once\n- `config/database.yml` reads everything from `ENV[\"DATABASE_URL\"]` — no hard-coded credentials\n- `start.sh` (executable) runs `bin/rails db:prepare` then serves `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground; README documents startup\n\n**Verified:** all endpoints via curl, odd JSON body shapes, boundary codes (4/20 chars), URL returned unchanged, creation-order listing, data surviving a server restart, and clean-state boot from a foreign cwd. Servers stopped, test rows wiped, port 8000 free for the harness."
